  "notes": "Candidate A (drawing fidelity). Scale 1.2 cm per photo pixel, anchored on the drawn corridor width (~230 px -> 280 cm). Room proportions and positions follow the sketch; only three rooms were bumped to the 400 cm minimum footprint (office_1 width 360->400, office_2 width 350->400, womens_restroom depth 300->400). Deviations forced by the schema: (1) the break room exit is a 120 cm door where the sketch runs the corridor straight into the room; (2) the sketch's single partial dividing wall becomes the reception|ceo_office wall with the door in the sketch's RIGHT-hand gap, plus a schema-required partial dividing wall inside the CEO office forming the west nook; (3) demon_1 is reserved at the Office #2 door mouth (sketch X is inside Office #2) and demon_2 inside the CEO office (sketch X is in reception); both drawn positions are kept as notes. The corridor is three rects joined by 'open' openings: corridor_blocked (collapse stub) | elevator_lobby (elevator on its north wall) | corridor_main; the passage to reception is corridor_south. The duct tube spans the 420 cm gap between the closet's south face (y=890) and the break room's north face (y=1310), passing through both walls. The window wall is declared only via money_shot.window_wall (no 'window' opening authored because there is no exterior room id). See Docs/candidates/floorplan_A.md.",
